WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.110
Good morning John.

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:03.520
My new office is set up over here.

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:09.019
We have the Games with Hank, and over here,
we have Vlogbrothers, and over here is my

00:00:09.019 --> 00:00:10.940
actual desk where I sit.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.639
This is just a picture of you.

00:00:12.639 --> 00:00:13.910
Oh it's your puff is a bird.

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:16.049
I'll put it full screen, so everybody can
see it.

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:21.140
Okay John, it's kind of easy to forget how
cool the things we get to do are.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:23.440
I get to have a channel where I just play
video games.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.360
You get to have a fictional soccer team...
that helps fund a real soccer team.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:30.910
We get to work in a new medium that, despite
what people who work in it say, no one understands

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:32.189
or knows what to do with.

00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:36.160
Crash Course is now being used as a tool in
literally thousands of schools.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:40.370
You got to hang out with Bill Gates, a guy
who would be the richest person in the world

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:46.220
if he hadn't given so much of his money away...
and just talk about the complexities of market

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:49.060
forces on rural agriculture in Ethiopia.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:50.060
What?

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:56.470
And in the last, like, four days, this community
has raised $260,000 to help people who don't

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:59.490
have access to clean water, get access to
clean water.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:03.380
I spent some time this week watching those
donations come in, and the most common thing

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:07.110
people say -- they get to leave a comment
if they want to -- is "I'm sorry I couldn't

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:08.110
give more."

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:12.440
And I don't spend enough time thinking about
how amazing this is -- just the weird and

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:16.710
wonderful position that has been granted to
us by two things:

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:22.720
One: pure, dumb luck, and two: the people
who are watching this right now.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:27.010
Just like I kinda get used to how I get to
do cool stuff now, people who are a part of

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:30.410
things or watch things forget that they're
the reason that the thing exists.

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:34.799
By spending time watching this video, you
are granting me power.

00:01:34.799 --> 00:01:38.880
And it's kinda weird to me that in a world
of infinite content, where there's 30 Rock

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:43.550
and Breaking Bad and PewDiePie and cat videos,
that you choose to watch this.

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:44.550
What-what-why?

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:46.740
Your time is a gift, and I am honored that
you give it to me.

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:48.720
But let's also have a little bit of real talk
here.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.320
I am still insecure.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:52.320
I still, like, get sad sometimes.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:58.140
And I don't struggle with depression, I don't
think; I just have a normal amount of sadness,

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:06.140
and sometimes I don't want to do stuff and
feel unmotivated and undeserving of the things

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:07.140
that I have.

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:09.989
And I think that's rational, like, I don't
-- there's nothing special about me that means

00:02:09.989 --> 00:02:11.330
that people should be watching me on the internet.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:15.530
I don't deserve it, but the thing that I don't
want to feel is that I'm faking it somehow.

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:19.220
Feeling like you don't deserve success, being
sad sometimes -- those are normal, but they're

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:22.070
not really socially acceptable to talk about,
so I figured bleeehh.

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:26.020
More socially acceptable is saying, "I"m so
overworked, I work all the time and I'm overwhelmed!"

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:27.040
which I AM!

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:31.100
There's a lot of things we could be doing
with our time and resources... but I don't

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.380
know what to do.

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:34.150
That decision is really hard.

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:37.440
It occurred to me today -- that's a lie, it
didn't occur to me; John actually said it

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:40.129
to me on the phone when we were talking -- that
I should just ask.

00:02:40.129 --> 00:02:43.790
You're the reason all of this exists; what
do you think we should do?

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:45.110
So I made a survey.

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:49.660
You can rank different things that we might
want to do in order of how much you think

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:53.370
we should do them, and then add if you have
other ideas for what we should do with the

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:54.370
power of this community.

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:58.069
That's, like, why didn't, like, what's wrong
with me that I didn't think of that before?!

00:02:58.069 --> 00:03:01.540
I have an amazing community that's supporting
all of the things we're doing, why don't I

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:04.170
ask them -- let you make the decision?

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:05.690
I don't want to!

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:06.690
That sounds hard!

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:10.130
So yeah, I was feeling a little down yesterday.

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:12.390
That happens, I think, to everyone...

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:13.610
I'm feeling better now.

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:20.300
On the list of things that I am grateful for
because of this thing, that's pretty high

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:21.300
up there.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:26.670
This is always there for me, to be a thing
that I need to do to motivate me, to get out

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:30.610
of bed, to make a thing, to be a part of something...
thanks.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:33.239
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

00:03:33.239 --> 00:03:39.900
And sometimes giant balls just appear!

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:45.600
It's a whole new, like, space-time thing.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.500
Oh my god, that was a big ball!

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:50.569
[Hank singing] Somebody once told me the world
is gonna roll me, I ain't the sharpest tool

00:03:50.569 --> 00:03:51.569
in the shed.

00:03:51.569 --> 00:03:52.569
Ahhhahahaha...

00:03:52.569 --> 00:03:53.569
Did you like that?

00:03:53.569 --> 00:03:54.569
You like Smash Mouth?

00:03:54.569 --> 00:03:55.569
Is that better?

00:03:55.569 --> 00:03:55.577
So have you ever seen the movie E.T.?

